   "unmapped": [
    "N clients interact round-robin each round with a star-shaped communication network through a central server; communication cost C_T = total number of times data is transferred",
    "Rewards from an exponential-family GLM with known scale; link mu is k_mu-Lipschitz with derivative >= c_mu on [-S,S]",
    "Noise is a martingale difference bounded by R_max (|eta| <= R_max)",
    "Algorithm uses k_mu (AGD step size) and R_max (confidence width)",
    "Each client has K arms per round"
   ],
   "definition_quote": "each client $i \\in [N]$ chooses an arm $\\bx_{t,i}$ from its time-varying candidate set ... the goal of the learning system is to minimize the cumulative (pseudo) regret over all $N$ clients ... $R_{T}=\\sum_{t=1}^{T} \\sum_{i=1}^{N}r_{t,i}$, where $r_{t,i}=\\max_{\\bx \\in \\cA_{t,i}} \\bbE[y|\\bx]- \\bbE[y_{t,i}|\\bx_{t,i}]$."
  }
